    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68244" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>toil</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱδρῶ θ᾽, ὃν ἵδρωσα μόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.27
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέθλους ἐξανύσαντα μόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.900
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόγῳ πολλῷ κάμηλον ἐξειλκύσαμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					1.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>trouble, distress</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1744
			</span></i> (lyr.). (Cf. Lith. <i>smagùs</i> 'heavy': the
			initial <i>s</i> is preserved in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμογερός,
				σμυγερός</span>.)</div>
